{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>El</b> — The name is strong, for [Elohim] illuminated us because in the morning the sacrifices are brought, not at night, and the priests say to Israel: bind the festival-offering — it is the lamb prepared for slaughter, like חגים ינקופו." "And the meaning is until it is brought near to the horns of the altar, on account of the tossing of the blood."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 118, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:05.017079672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}